  **STRING METHODS**

1.length()	
->Returns the length of a string.	
"Hello".length() → 5
2.charAt()	
->Returns a character at a given index.
"Hello".charAt(1) → e
3.toUpperCase()
->Converts to uppercase.	
"hello".toUpperCase() → HELLO
4.toLowerCase()	
->Converts to lowercase.	
"HELLO".toLowerCase() → hello
5.equals()
->Compares two strings.	
"Java".equals("Java") → true
6.equalsIgnoreCase()	
->Compares strings ignoring case.	
"Java".equalsIgnoreCase("JAVA") → true
7.concat()
->Joins two strings.
"Hello".concat(" World")
8.substring()	
->Extracts part of a string.	
"Hello".substring(1,4) → ell
9.contains()
->Checks whether text is present.	
"Hello".contains("ell") → true
10.indexOf()	
->Returns the position of a character or text.	
"Hello".indexOf('l') → 2
11.replace()
->Replaces characters or text.
"Hello".replace('l','p') → Heppo
12.trim()	
->Removes leading and trailing spaces.
" Hi ".trim() → Hi
13.startsWith()	
->Checks the beginning of a string.	
"Java".startsWith("Ja") → true
14.endsWith()
->Checks the ending of a string.	
"Java".endsWith("va") → true
15.isEmpty()	
->Checks whether a string is empty.	
"".isEmpty() → true
    
